WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.660
An old earl holds a
letter: "If it be nothing,

2
00:00:03.710 --> 00:00:05.770
I shall not need spectacles."

3
00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.800
His eyes work perfectly.

4
00:00:07.850 --> 00:00:10.730
And he believes every forged word.

5
00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:13.100
Later, he cannot see at all.

6
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:16.210
Yet he says, "I stumbled when I saw."

7
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:18.180
With eyes, he was fooled.

8
00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.430
Without them, he finds the truth.

9
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.010
How can that be?

10
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.140
In this mission, you'll
count the eyes in this play,

11
00:00:25.190 --> 00:00:27.810
from Kent's first-scene
warning: "See better,

12
00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.930
Lear;" You'll read Gloucester's
words on the heath,

13
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:32.580
one line at a time.

14
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:37.310
And you'll meet three kinds of
madness, and hear what the mad can see.

15
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:41.720
Your mission: explain how a
blind man comes to see the truth.
